00:19:23.129 --> 00:19:26.659
Now after the second half life,
you're going to divide that by

00:19:26.679 --> 00:19:28.159
in half again, so 32 micrograms.

00:19:28.524 --> 00:19:34.254
Divide by two, and then we'll have
a total of 16 micrograms, and that's

00:19:34.254 --> 00:19:39.244
going to be how much is left and
remaining with inside your sample.

00:19:39.604 --> 00:19:42.084
So it's all about, well,
how much is active?

00:19:42.104 --> 00:19:45.794
It's going to be 16 micrograms,
and it went through two half

00:19:45.814 --> 00:19:46.874
lives when that happened.

00:19:47.325 --> 00:19:50.895
And so essentially you can kind of
see is that each part, right, we had

00:19:50.895 --> 00:19:56.285
a half of our at the middle, and now
we're down to a quarter of our sample

00:19:56.325 --> 00:19:58.955
after the second half life, and then
if you went through another one, it'd

00:19:58.965 --> 00:20:02.465
be at an eighth, then a sixteenth,
then a thirty second, and so forth.

00:20:02.474 --> 00:20:04.684
It's gonna keep getting smaller
and smaller and smaller.

