So what's actually
occurring within the bomb?

00:24:27.230 --> 00:24:28.590
What do they actually have?

00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:32.230
Well, the whole idea is that
inside of it, there is a bunch

00:24:32.230 --> 00:24:34.090
of uranium that is inside.

00:24:34.410 --> 00:24:38.280
And this is a essentially to uranium 235.

00:24:38.779 --> 00:24:41.350
And then it's just it's
sitting inside the container.

00:24:41.370 --> 00:24:44.070
It's not going to do
anything just being in there.

00:24:44.399 --> 00:24:46.420
The thing is, it needs to be activated.

00:24:46.770 --> 00:24:48.780
Now how is that actually done?

00:24:49.129 --> 00:24:54.230
Well, what it, what happens is
they essentially shoot a neutron.

00:24:54.705 --> 00:24:57.605
at the uranium atom or isotope.

00:24:58.195 --> 00:25:01.135
When that happens, then
it becomes unstable.

00:25:01.145 --> 00:25:05.025
The entire thing cannot
last in this condition.

00:25:05.035 --> 00:25:09.455
It's going to explode and release
a ton of energy as a result.

00:25:09.875 --> 00:25:13.615
So once that neutron gets shot in
there, it's going to be really unstable.

00:25:13.615 --> 00:25:16.435
And the goal is to make stable isotopes.

00:25:16.955 --> 00:25:22.115
So it's going to split into two
different, completely different isotopes.

00:25:22.655 --> 00:25:28.475
And in the process release three
different neutrons as a result.

00:25:29.024 --> 00:25:31.074
Now is that something
that's so crazy, right?

00:25:31.074 --> 00:25:34.504
It releases a ton of energy
as a result, but is that all?

00:25:34.915 --> 00:25:38.634
Well, essentially the way that that
works when it comes to a bomb is

00:25:38.834 --> 00:25:40.484
it's all about a chain reaction.

00:25:40.844 --> 00:25:43.945
And the same thing if you want to
actually cause a nuclear reaction

00:25:43.945 --> 00:25:46.165
within a reactor to produce energy.

00:25:46.555 --> 00:25:49.125
It's all about, well,
once I have the first one.

00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:54.450
Can I have the reaction keep going
right where it keeps increasing, right?

00:25:54.450 --> 00:25:58.310
So if one goes and they release
neutrons spontaneously, can it

00:25:58.310 --> 00:26:00.290
hit another set of uraniums?

00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:04.860
Which will then cause it to cascade
and cause More of these different

00:26:04.869 --> 00:26:08.339
elements to split releasing more
neutrons and that will keep going

00:26:08.379 --> 00:26:12.155
over and over and over again Have in
many of these different reactions.

00:26:12.515 --> 00:26:18.075
So what the whole idea is when it comes to
