00:26:18.075 --> 00:26:22.465
the rapid increase in the number of high
energy neutrons that are created, right?

00:26:22.465 --> 00:26:26.524
So every time when you have one, it
will split into three, which will

00:26:26.535 --> 00:26:28.214
split into another set of three.

00:26:28.495 --> 00:26:31.345
So you can kind of see it's
like a cube function of how fast

00:26:31.345 --> 00:26:32.675
this thing is going to grow.

00:26:33.235 --> 00:26:36.315
Now, in order to sustain this reaction.

00:26:36.715 --> 00:26:40.355
All the uranium must be brought to
very, very close together, right?

00:26:40.355 --> 00:26:44.485
So if you think of like the uranium,
uh, nuclear bomb, it was all kept in a

00:26:44.485 --> 00:26:49.284
very, very tight capsule in order for
it to go very, very fast and release

00:26:49.284 --> 00:26:50.935
a ton of energy all at the same time.

00:26:51.504 --> 00:26:54.134
So now, when it's all brought
together, this is what's

00:26:54.134 --> 00:26:56.394
