00:28:54.245 --> 00:28:58.365
So the whole idea with this reaction
is when you take isotopes of hydrogen

00:28:58.675 --> 00:29:00.705
and they, then they react together.

00:29:01.025 --> 00:29:05.235
So if you didn't realize there are three
different major isotopes of hydrogen,

00:29:05.255 --> 00:29:09.125
there's the normal one with just one
proton, but there's also deuterium,

00:29:09.175 --> 00:29:13.645
which has an atomic mass of two as one
neutron, and then tritium, which has two

00:29:13.645 --> 00:29:16.165
neutrons and then the one proton to it.

00:29:16.485 --> 00:29:19.705
So when tritium and
deuterium combine together.

00:29:20.055 --> 00:29:23.875
They're going to make a helium
atom and release a neutron and

00:29:23.875 --> 00:29:25.725
a ton of energy in the process.

00:29:26.145 --> 00:29:28.874
Now with that, that is what
the whole idea of fusion is.

